.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt XO-LEXICON 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xo-lexicon
.Nd build, merge, and check the libxo lexicon of tag names
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm build
.Fl p Ar package
.Op Fl o Ar dir
.Op Fl d Ar discouraged.lex
.Ar source ...
.Nm
.Cm merge
.Op Fl D Ar dir
.Nm
.Cm check
.Op Fl D Ar dir
.Op Fl n
.Ar source ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The lexicon records the tag names (element and member names) that
installed programs use in their libxo output, so that new
programs can reuse common names instead of inventing synonyms.
.Pp
The lexicon directory holds one pair of files for each package:
.Bl -tag -width "pkg.discouraged.lex"
.It Pa pkg.lex
The tags the package uses, one per line, as
.Dq tag count ,
where count is the number of places in the source that use the tag.
.It Pa pkg.discouraged.lex
Tags the package has shipped but whose continued use should be
limited, as
.Dq tag Op replacement .
A tag that was never shipped but should never be used is a
discouraged tag with a count of zero.
.El
.Pp
.Cm merge
combines the per-package files into two files, which are a cache
and are never edited:
.Bl -tag -width "system.discouraged.lex"
.It Pa system.lex
.Dq tag packages uses ,
where packages is the number of packages that use the tag, and
uses is the total number of uses.
.It Pa system.discouraged.lex
.Dq tag packages uses Op replacement .
When packages disagree on the replacement, the first one (in file
name order) is kept and a warning is given.
.El
.Pp
In all files, text after
.Dq #
is a comment and blank lines are ignored.
.Ss Modes
.Bl -tag -width "check"
.It Cm build
Run at build time.
Writes
.Pa package.lex
into
.Ar dir
(default
.Dq . ) ,
using
.Xr xolint 1
.Fl L
over the sources.
With
.Fl d ,
copies the hand-maintained
.Ar discouraged.lex
to
.Pa package.discouraged.lex .
.It Cm merge
Run from a package's post-install and post-deinstall hooks.
Rebuilds
.Pa system.lex
and
.Pa system.discouraged.lex
from the per-package files present in the directory.
Since the result depends only on the directory's contents, a
reinstall or an uninstall needs nothing more.
.It Cm check
Reports each tag the sources use as
.Dq known ,
.Dq discouraged
(with its replacement, if any), or
.Dq new ,
with the number of uses in the sources and the number of packages
that use it.
With
.Fl n ,
prints only the new tags, one per line, which is the new-words file
of a conversion.
If any per-package file is newer than
.Pa system.lex ,
the files are merged in memory first, so a missed hook does no harm.
.El
.Pp
.Fl D Ar dir
names the lexicon directory; the default is the installed one.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "XOLINT"
.It Ev XOLINT
The
.Xr xolint 1
to run; the default is the installed one.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
% xo-lexicon build -p wc -d discouraged.lex wc.c
% xo-lexicon merge
% xo-lexicon check -n wc.c > wc.new-words
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xolint 1 ,
.Xr xo_emit 3 ,
.Xr libxo 3
